    <worksheet name='Return Rate by State'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Geographic Distribution of Return Rates Across the U.S.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='10'>This map shows that return rates vary by state and are not solely driven by sales volume. Some states have disproportionately high return rates, indicating potential regional issues affecting customer satisfaction or product performance. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='10'>While some states such as Utah show the highest return rates, these may be driven by smaller order volumes. In contrast, larger states like California combine both high return rates and high sales volume, making them a more significant contributor to overall returns. This suggests that return issues are influenced by both regional behavior and order volume. </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
