    <worksheet name='Return Rate by State and Category'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Return Rate by State and Category</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='10'>This treemap shows that return rates are not uniformly distributed across categories or regions, but instead are concentrated within specific category–state combinations. Technology products exhibit the highest return rates across several states, suggesting potential issues with product quality, expectations, or fit. Office Supplies also show elevated return rates in select regions, while Furniture demonstrates more moderate and evenly distributed return behavior. This indicates that return drivers are a combination of both product characteristics and geographic factors.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Orders+ (Superstore)' name='federated.1s83zia08yjbxn1fv2opk1idhrvf' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.1s83zia08yjbxn1fv2opk1idhrvf'>
            <column caption='Returned Flag' datatype='integer' default-format='p0%' name='[Calculation_1395888384012288]' role='measure' type='quantitative'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='IF [Returned] = &quot;Yes&quot; THEN 1&#13;&#10;ELSE 0&#13;&#10;END' />
            </column>
            <column datatype='string' name='[Category]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column datatype='string' name='[Region]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
