              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='94087' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98426' x='787' y='5083'>
              <zone h='10477' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98426' x='787' y='5083' />
              <zone h='83610' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98426' x='787' y='15560'>
                <flipboard active-id='7' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                  <story-points>
                    <story-point caption='What Is Driving Returns at Superstore' captured-sheet='' id='1' />
                    <story-point caption='How Returns Are Measured&#9;' captured-sheet='' id='2' />
                    <story-point caption='High Return Rates Concentrated in Western States, Led by Utah and California' captured-sheet='Return Rate by State' id='3'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <worksheet name='Return Rate by State'>
                          <style delta-type='added'>
                            <style-rule element='axis'>
                              <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.1s83zia08yjbxn1fv2opk1idhrvf].[Latitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='7846034.8015725818' min='1314722.8262065905' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='rows' type='space' />
                              <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.1s83zia08yjbxn1fv2opk1idhrvf].[Longitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='-7428956.9370736051' min='-14241719.655143751' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='cols' type='space' />
                            </style-rule>
                          </style>
                        </worksheet>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='Return Rates Spike in August and Late-Year Months' captured-sheet='Return Rate by Month' id='4'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <worksheet name='Return Rate by Month'>
                          <style delta-type='added'>
                            <style-rule element='axis'>
                              <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.1s83zia08yjbxn1fv2opk1idhrvf].[mn:Order Date:qk]' field-type='quantitative' scope='cols' type='space' />
                            </style-rule>
                          </style>
                          <selection-collection>
                            <node-selection select-tuples='false'>
                              <oriented-node-reference orientation='horizontal'>
                                <node-reference>
                                  <axis>[federated.1s83zia08yjbxn1fv2opk1idhrvf].[mn:Order Date:qk]</axis>
                                </node-reference>
                                <page-reference />
                              </oriented-node-reference>
                            </node-selection>
                          </selection-collection>
                        </worksheet>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='Technology Has the Highest Return Rate, but Differences Are Small Across Categories' captured-sheet='Return Rate by Category' id='5' />
                    <story-point caption='High Return Volume Is Concentrated in High-Selling Sub-Categories' captured-sheet='Sales vs Returns by Sub-Category' id='6' />
                    <story-point caption='Conclusion' captured-sheet='' id='7' />
                  </story-points>
                </flipboard>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='63071' hidden='true' id='10' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='93898' x='2756' y='15145'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>Join me on a journey through the world of data visualization, covering everything from bar charts to scatter plots. Throughout this presentation, I encourage you to critically evaluate how we can leverage these visual insights to reduce our overall return rates. Identifying the key drivers of product returns and providing actionable insights to reduce return rates. I am going to take you on a little journey we will be looking at various types of graphs from maps, bar charts to scatter plots. We will be looking into different scenarios all while in the back of your mind I want you to think what can we do better at in some of the key points we will talk about in this presentation.   </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='32158' hidden='true' id='11' story-point-id='2' type-v2='text' w='91535' x='5020' y='23237'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='16'>Returns can be measured in multiple ways, including total returns, return rate, and financial impact. In this analysis, return rate is used as the primary metric because it provides a normalized view of returns relative to total orders, making it easier to compare across categories, regions, and time.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='10581' hidden='true' id='12' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='77264' x='3248' y='17427'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Return rates are highest in western states such as Utah, Oregon, and California, indicating potential operational or product issues. In contrast, states like Nebraska and Indiana show very low return rates. The company should investigate high-return regions and apply successful strategies from low-return areas.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='23444' hidden='true' id='13' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='34055' x='9449' y='19398'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Return rates peak in August, remain elevated through fall, drop in November, and rise again in December. This suggests returns follow major purchasing periods, indicating a delay between purchases and returns.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='13382' hidden='true' id='14' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='70079' x='6299' y='31639'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Technology products have the highest return rate among all categories, making them the primary contributor to returns. However, the differences between categories are relatively small, suggesting that return behavior is not driven by category alone and requires deeper analysis at the product level.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='14419' hidden='true' id='15' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='77461' x='13287' y='34232'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>The most important insight from product-level analysis is that return volume is concentrated in high-selling sub-categories such as Phones, Binders, and Paper. These products generate the largest number of returns primarily due to their high sales volume. This indicates that overall return impact is driven more by product popularity than return rate alone, and these high-volume items should be prioritized for operational improvements.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='35477' id='16' story-point-id='7' type-v2='text' w='83661' x='9350' y='26763'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Returns are not evenly distributed across the business and are primarily driven by a small number of high-impact factors. High return volume is concentrated in high-selling sub-categories such as Phones, Binders, and Paper, while elevated return rates are observed in specific regions and during peak seasonal periods like August and late-year months. This indicates that returns are driven by product popularity, geography, and purchasing cycles rather than a single root cause. To reduce returns, the company should prioritize improvements in high-volume products, investigate operational issues in high-return regions, and prepare for seasonal spikes through better inventory planning and customer expectation management. </run>
            <run fontalignment='0' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>By focusing on these targeted areas, the company can significantly reduce return-related costs and improve overall customer satisfaction. </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{502D0E22-3ADA-4B63-8FB9-E074517E4D02}' />
    </dashboard>
